<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Machine Learning - Tag - 0make</title><link>https://0make.top/tags/machine-learning/</link><description>This is my new Hugo FixIt site</description><generator>Hugo 0.168.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><managingEditor>0make@gmail.com (AZ)</managingEditor><webMaster>0make@gmail.com (AZ)</webMaster><lastBuildDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:58:50 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://0make.top/tags/machine-learning/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Supervised Learning</title><link>https://0make.top/resources/ai/sl/</link><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0800</pubDate><author>0make@gmail.com (AZ)</author><guid>https://0make.top/resources/ai/sl/</guid><category domain="https://0make.top/categories/ai/">AI</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Supervised Learning is one of the three core paradigms of machine learning (the other two being unsupervised learning and reinforcement learning). It is currently the most widely used and mature machine learning method.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 class="heading-element" id="-what-is-supervised-learning"&gt;&lt;span&gt;🎓 What is Supervised Learning?&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#-what-is-supervised-learning" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supervised Learning&lt;/strong&gt; is a machine learning method that uses &lt;strong&gt;labeled datasets&lt;/strong&gt; to train algorithms, allowing the model to learn the mapping relationship between inputs and outputs.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Unsupervised Learning</title><link>https://0make.top/resources/ai/usl/</link><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0800</pubDate><author>0make@gmail.com (AZ)</author><guid>https://0make.top/resources/ai/usl/</guid><category domain="https://0make.top/categories/ai/">AI</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Unsupervised Learning is another core paradigm of machine learning, forming a sharp contrast with supervised learning.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 class="heading-element" id="what-is-unsupervised-learning"&gt;&lt;span&gt;What is Unsupervised Learning?&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#what-is-unsupervised-learning" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 class="heading-element" id="-one-sentence-definition"&gt;&lt;span&gt;📝 One-Sentence Definition&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;a href="#-one-sentence-definition" class="heading-mark"&gt;&#10; &lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;path d="m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unsupervised Learning&lt;/strong&gt; is a machine learning method that discovers hidden patterns, structures, or relationships in &lt;strong&gt;unlabeled data&lt;/strong&gt; without requiring人工标注.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Reinforcement Learning (RL) Development History</title><link>https://0make.top/resources/ai/rl/</link><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0800</pubDate><author>0make@gmail.com (AZ)</author><guid>https://0make.top/resources/ai/rl/</guid><category domain="https://0make.top/categories/ai/">AI</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Reinforcement Learning (RL) is one of the three core paradigms of machine learning (alongside supervised learning and unsupervised learning).&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Its core idea is: &lt;strong&gt;An agent learns the optimal policy through trial and error by interacting with the environment, based on reward or penalty signals&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Throughout the history of AI development, reinforcement learning has undergone several major paradigm shifts, evolving from early mathematical theoretical derivations to becoming the core engine driving large language models and embodied AI today.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>